From: b70-notes <b70-notes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:32:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] SYCL MUL_MAT_ID small batches: experimental
 shared-expert kernel (GGML_SYCL_MMID_DEDUP=1, off) and GGML_SYCL_MMID_STATS

- GGML_SYCL_MMID_DEDUP=1: 2-8 token batches in one launch; a planning kernel marks, per (token, slot), whether an
  earlier token routes to the same expert, and the owner computes that expert's rows for every token using it
  (Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 reordered layouts, Q5_0 through local memory). Bit-identical results (PPL equal, MUL_MAT_ID
  q4_K/q5_0/q8_0/q6_K/q5_K 242/242). Not faster: real text -ub 4 -1.6 % pass time, -ub 2 +3.5 %; default off.
- GGML_SYCL_MMID_STATS=N (debug, host sync): distinct experts per small batch. Inkling 2 Mini uncensored on real text:
  adjacent tokens share 3.3 of 8 experts; distinct/slots 0.79 at 2 tokens, 0.62 at 4.

